    "description": "Preflight the two opaque UUID128 custom face-property chunks before the atomic OpenMesh read; zero-byte istream input returns Empty without replacement, matching the historical vector path.",
    "scanner": "Uses upstream OMFormat Header/Chunk/PropertyName and IO::restore. Names are read only at chunk boundaries, never searched in payload. Requires each identity property at most once, Face/Custom entity/type, uint64_t storage type, exact 8*n_faces block size and payload within original bytes; both absent remains legacy.",
    "sizes": "Parent-reviewed OMFormat::scalar_size has integer/float widths inverted. Uses IO::size_of and original Float_Size/Integer_Size enum meanings. Float32/64 supported, Float128 rejected because upstream position/normal reader does not support it; no sizeof(long double) assumption.",
    "legacy": "Original bytes remain unchanged and seed the deterministic identity. Indexed-face topology before OM2.0 follows the upstream framing branch; complete-chunk EOF through OM2.1 follows the old reader behavior. OM2.2 requires final sentinel. These old-version paths have not received native artifact validation.",
    "zeroHalf": "No rejection of zero halves; only the complete null UUID is invalid."
  },
  "regressions": {
    "status": "AUTHORED_BEFORE_FIX_RED_NOT_RUN_GREEN_NOT_RUN",
    "added": [
